# Continuous 30m Forest Canopy Height for Yunnan Province (1986–2023)

## 📌 Overview
This repository contains the Google Earth Engine (GEE) JavaScript code used to generate a continuous 30m resolution forest canopy height dataset for Yunnan Province, China, spanning from 1986 to 2023.

The code processes multi-source remote sensing data (e.g., Landsat time series, GEDI, ICESat-2) to produce a wall-to-wall canopy height map. 

## 📂 Repository Structure
- `CanopyHeight_Yunnan_1986_2023.js`: The main GEE script.
- `README.md`: Project description and instructions.
- `LICENSE`: License information.

## 🚀 How to Use
1. Go to [Google Earth Engine Code Editor](https://code.earthengine.google.com/).
2. Copy the content of `CanopyHeight_Yunnan_1986_2023.js` and paste it into the editor.
3. Ensure you have the necessary assets (e.g., GEDI L2A/L4A, Landsat) imported in your GEE environment.
4. Click "Run" to execute the script.

